msgid "``main``"
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main:1 of
msgid "Application entry point."
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main:3 of
msgid "This module contains utility functions that handle start-up of the Glasgow CLI as well as custom applications based on the Glasgow API. To begin building your application, copy the following example:"
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main.setup_logging:1 of
msgid "Configure logging."
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main.setup_logging:3 of
msgid "The ANSI escape sequences used to colorize the output can be customized via the :envvar:`GLASGOW_COLORS` environment variable. Its value must contain a ``:``-delimited list of ``<key>=<value>`` pairs, where ``<key>`` is one of ``TRACE``, ``DEBUG``, ``INFO``, ``WARNING``, ``ERROR``, ``CRITICAL``, ``RESET``, and ``<value>`` is used as the core of an escape sequence :py:`\"\\033[<value>m\"`."
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main.setup_logging:9 of
msgid "For example, to make messages with the ``TRACE`` level gray and messages with the ``INFO`` level white, set ``GLASGOW_COLORS`` to ``TRACE=37:INFO=1;37``."
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main.setup_logging:12 of
msgid "A :class:`logging.StreamHandler` writing to :data:`sys.stderr` is created, attached to the root logger, and returned."
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main.run_async:1 of
msgid "Configure the runtime and call :py:`main`."
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main.run_async:3 of
msgid "This decorator is used as a convenient way to use the Glasgow library in your own scripts. The :py:`main` function called from a new :mod:`asyncio` event loop after applying any necessary workarounds for platform and library quirks."
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main.run_async:7 of
msgid "Moreover, if the file with the :meth:`run_async` decorator is directly invoked from the command line (as opposed to being imported), it also calls the wrapped :py:`main` function, as if that file includes the following code immediately after the definition of :py:`main`:"
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main.run_async_qtqml:1 glasgow.main.run_async_qtwidgets:1 of
msgid "Configure the Qt runtime and call :py:`main`."
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main.run_async_qtwidgets:3 of
msgid "This decorator serves the same purpose as :func:`run_async` and works the same way, except that it initializes a graphical application using the QtWidgets library."
msgstr ""

#: glasgow.main.run_async_qtqml:3 of
msgid "This decorator serves the same purpose as :func:`run_async` and works the same way, except that it initializes a graphical application using the QtQml library."
msgstr ""

